                <pb facs="0601" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg491"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5662: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-17T15:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1928—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:14 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>218. My May 16, 6 p.m. Newspaper reports indicate that the Chamorro members of
                    the Conservative directorate at the meeting referred to in my May 16, 6 p.m.,
                    and at a second meeting held yesterday completed the work of passing upon the
                    credentials of the delegates to the National Convention.</p>
                <p>They also elected Doctor Ignacio Suarez as alternate to the Conservative
                    political member of the National Board of Elections. The President informed me
                    this morning that he would not recognize the validity of any action taken by the
                    directorate at these meetings because they had been illegally called.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
